    title: "Saudi-led coalition dismisses ‘misleading’ Houthi claim of Riyadh attack",
    summary: "The Saudi-led coalition spokesman says the Yemeni armed group is 'attempting to divert attention' from its losses.",
    preview: "The Saudi-led coalition spokesman says the Yemeni armed group is ‘attempting to divert attention’ from its losses. Saudi-backed Yemeni army says 700 Houthis killed in 24 hours The Houthis’ claims that the Iran-allied armed group has targeted Saudi Arabia’s capital Riyadh are “misleading”, according to the Saudi-led coalition supporting Yemen’s internationally recognised government. Coalition spokesman Turki al-Maliki’s remarks came on Saturday after the Houthis claimed ballistic missile and drone attacks on an Aramco oil facility near Riyadh.",
    body: "The Saudi-led coalition spokesman says the Yemeni armed group is ‘attempting to divert attention’ from its losses.\n\nSaudi-backed Yemeni army says 700 Houthis killed in 24 hours\n\nThe Houthis’ claims that the Iran-allied armed group has targeted Saudi Arabia’s capital Riyadh are “misleading”, according to the Saudi-led coalition supporting Yemen’s internationally recognised government.\n\nCoalition spokesman Turki al-Maliki’s remarks came on Saturday after the Houthis claimed ballistic missile and drone attacks on an Aramco oil facility near Riyadh.\n\nRecommended Stories\n\nlist of 4 items\n\n- list 1 of 4Yemen’s army says targets Houthis in hundreds of strikes, killing 700\n\n- list 2 of 4A Yemeni family spends a week on the road fleeing another Houthi offensive\n\n- list 3 of 4Somalia won’t accept Israeli presence ‘under any circumstances’: President\n\n- list 4 of 4Houthis claim strike on Aramco site as Yemen fighting intensifies\n\nThe group said the assault caused large fires as fighting between the Houthis and government forces intensifies in Yemen.\n\nIn remarks carried by Saudi media Asharq Al-Awsat late on Saturday, al-Maliki claimed that the Houthis are “attempting to divert attention from the scale of the losses and the growing public anger against them”.\n\n‘Chaos and devastation’\n\nThe development comes after the Yemeni forces “executed 257 precision targeting operations” against Houthi sites, movements, and military capabilities on Saturday, according to the spokesman for Yemen’s internationally recognised government forces, Colonel Majed Abdullah al-Nazili.\n\nHe added that initial estimates indicate that the operations killed at least 700 Houthi rebels.\n\nMeanwhile, al-Maliki said the Houthis’ “ties to external agendas” have brought “chaos and devastation to Yemen”, adding that “what the Houthis are facing in Taiz … drive them to seek illusory victories”.\n\nEarly on Sunday, the Saudi-led coalition said its armed forces carried out 97 “precise targeting operations” against Houthi reinforcements on the Tor al-Baha front and the Taiz axis, using warplanes, drones, artillery, missiles and snipers.\n\nThe fighting between the Houthis and Yemeni government forces has intensified since a fragile 2022 truce collapsed in July, displacing hundreds of thousands of people since then.\n\nIn mid-September, the Houthis seized the port city of Mocha and strategic islands in the Bab al-Mandeb strait, a vital route for global oil shipments, before anti-Houthi forces stabilised front lines.\n\nYemen has been at war since the Houthis seized the capital Sanaa in 2014, forcing the Yemeni government to retreat to Aden.",
    content_status: "full",
    source: "Al Jazeera",
    url: "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/4/houthi-claims-of-targeting-riyadh-are-misleading-saudi-led?traffic_source=rss",
